Examples for the ILVES bond/angle constraint solver.

ILVES is invoked via "fix ilves".  The fix gathers the complete bond /
angle topology onto every MPI rank at init via MPI_Allgatherv and
builds a per-rank constraint list including every cluster intersecting
the rank's local atoms.  This supports arbitrarily large connected
constraint clusters (e.g. all C-C backbone bonds of a long polymer
chain held in a single cluster) and any cluster topology -- including
chains, rings, branched stars, or fully connected meshes.

Selectors and keywords mirror fix shake: the fix shake form

    fix cstr all shake 1.0e-4 25 0 b 4 6 8 10 12 14 18 a 31

becomes

    fix cstr all ilves 1.0e-4 25 0 b 4 6 8 10 12 14 18 a 31

Two solver variants are available via the *variant* keyword:
  * variant = fast (default): symmetric Jacobian using r_k.r_l in
    off-diagonals; solved with banded Cholesky on an RCM-permuted
    matrix, and the factor is cached and reused across Newton
    iterations within a step.  Up to ~5x faster than the full variant
    on the all-backbone polymer / protein benchmark.
  * variant = full: the structurally-symmetric exact Newton Jacobian
    using s_k.r_l in off-diagonals; solved with LU.  Required when
    the constraint geometry has degenerate clusters that the
    Cholesky path cannot factor (the solver will fall back to LU per
    cluster as needed, but starting in "full" mode skips the
    fallback overhead).

Both variants converge to the exact solution of the constraint
equations.

For near-linear angle constraints (theta_0 close to 180 deg, common
in coarse-grain polymer backbones), use the *linearangle* keyword to
switch the angle's constraint topology from {AB, BC, AC} (which is
rank-deficient at exactly 180 deg) to {AB, AC, B-M} where M is the
midpoint of the A-C virtual bond:

    fix cstr all ilves 1.0e-5 30 0 b 1 a 1 variant fast linearangle 165

Default threshold is 165 deg; set to 180 to disable.

Example input files:
  in.peptide-fast     -- peptide + water with ilves, symmetric variant (fast)
  in.peptide-full     -- peptide + water with ilves, exact-Newton variant (full)
  in.peptide-mix      -- peptide groups via ilves, water via fix shake
  in.peptide-allbonds -- ilves constraining ALL bonds, demonstrating
                         arbitrarily-large connected bonds cluster support
  in.peptide-shake    -- baseline using fix shake for comparison
  in.peptide-rattle   -- baseline using fix rattle for comparison
  in.rhodo-fast       -- rhodopsin with same constraints (fast)
  in.rhodo-full       -- rhodopsin with C-H bonds + H-O-H water angle (full)
  in.rhodo-allbonds   -- rhodopsin with all bonds + water angle
  in.bulk_co2         -- bulk CO2 fluid (rigid linear; see comments in manual
                         for caveats on exactly-180 deg symmetric angles)
  in.cg-polymer       -- coarse-grain polymer chain with near-180 deg
                         backbone angles; demonstrates the *linearangle*
                         keyword in its intended regime
